q q 1 0 0 1 78 719.8898 cm 0 0 0 rg BT 22 TL/F2 18 Tf 1 0 0 1 0 26 Tm (PL/SQL Practical No. 11 - Stored Function for)Tj T* (Addition)Tj T* ET Q q 1 0 0 1 78 111.4898 cm 0 0 0 rg BT 8.8 TL/F3 8 Tf 1 0 0 1 36 572.8 Tm (QUESTION:)Tj T* T* (Create a stored function that accepts 2 numbers and returns the )Tj T* (addition of passed values. Also, write the code to call your function.)Tj T* T* (------------------------------------------------------------)Tj T* (STEP 1: CREATE FUNCTION)Tj T* (------------------------------------------------------------)Tj T* T* (CREATE OR REPLACE FUNCTION Add_Numbers\()Tj T* (    num1 IN NUMBER,)Tj T* (    num2 IN NUMBER)Tj T* (\) RETURN NUMBER)Tj T* (IS)Tj T* (    result NUMBER;)Tj T* (BEGIN)Tj T* (    result := num1 + num2;)Tj T* (    RETURN result;)Tj T* (END;)Tj T* (/)Tj T* T* (OUTPUT:)Tj T* (Function Created.)Tj T* T* (------------------------------------------------------------)Tj T* (STEP 2: CALL FUNCTION USING PL/SQL BLOCK)Tj T* (------------------------------------------------------------)Tj T* T* (SET SERVEROUTPUT ON;)Tj T* T* (DECLARE)Tj T* (    v_result NUMBER;)Tj T* (BEGIN)Tj T* (    v_result := Add_Numbers\(10, 20\);)Tj T* (    DBMS_OUTPUT.PUT_LINE\('Addition Result: ' || v_result\);)Tj T* (END;)Tj T* (/)Tj T* T* (------------------------------------------------------------)Tj T* (EXPECTED OUTPUT:)Tj T* T* (Addition Result: 30)Tj T* T* (------------------------------------------------------------)Tj T* (STEP 3: CALL FUNCTION USING SELECT STATEMENT)Tj T* (------------------------------------------------------------)Tj T* T* (SELECT Add_Numbers\(15, 25\) AS Result FROM DUAL;)Tj T* T* (------------------------------------------------------------)Tj T* (EXPECTED OUTPUT:)Tj T* T* (Result)Tj T* (------)Tj T* (40)Tj T* T* (------------------------------------------------------------)Tj T* (VIVA POINTS:)Tj T* T* (1. Function must return a value using RETURN keyword.)Tj T* (2. IN parameter is used to pass values to function.)Tj T* (3. DUAL is a dummy table used in Oracle.)Tj T* (4. Stored function can be called inside SELECT statement.)Tj T* (5. Difference between Procedure and Function:)Tj T* (   - Function returns value.)Tj T* (   - Procedure may or may not return value.)Tj T* ET Q Q q 0 0 612 792 re W n BT 9.6 TL/F18ae6e415-71a2-4778-8cc8-a7c717c03d28 8 Tf 1 0 0 1 511.352 777.6 Tm T* ET Q
