q q 1 0 0 1 78 719.8898 cm 0 0 0 rg BT 22 TL/F2 18 Tf 1 0 0 1 0 26 Tm (PL/SQL Practical No. 15 - Reverse String Using)Tj T* (PL/SQL Block)Tj T* ET Q q 1 0 0 1 78 357.8898 cm 0 0 0 rg BT 8.8 TL/F3 8 Tf 1 0 0 1 36 326.4 Tm (QUESTION:)Tj T* T* (Write a program to reverse a string using PL/SQL block.)Tj T* T* (------------------------------------------------------------)Tj T* (STEP 1: PL/SQL BLOCK)Tj T* (------------------------------------------------------------)Tj T* T* (SET SERVEROUTPUT ON;)Tj T* T* (DECLARE)Tj T* (    v_string VARCHAR2\(50\) := 'BHAVESH';)Tj T* (    v_reverse VARCHAR2\(50\) := '';)Tj T* (    i NUMBER;)Tj T* (BEGIN)Tj T* (    FOR i IN REVERSE 1..LENGTH\(v_string\) LOOP)Tj T* (        v_reverse := v_reverse || SUBSTR\(v_string, i, 1\);)Tj T* (    END LOOP;)Tj T* T* (    DBMS_OUTPUT.PUT_LINE\('Original String: ' || v_string\);)Tj T* (    DBMS_OUTPUT.PUT_LINE\('Reversed String: ' || v_reverse\);)Tj T* (END;)Tj T* (/)Tj T* T* (------------------------------------------------------------)Tj T* (EXPECTED OUTPUT:)Tj T* T* (Original String: BHAVESH)Tj T* (Reversed String: HSEVAHB)Tj T* T* (------------------------------------------------------------)Tj T* (VIVA POINTS:)Tj T* T* (1. LENGTH\(\) returns length of string.)Tj T* (2. SUBSTR\(\) extracts character from string.)Tj T* (3. REVERSE loop runs from last position to first.)Tj T* (4. || operator is used for string concatenation.)Tj T* (5. DBMS_OUTPUT.PUT_LINE displays output.)Tj T* ET Q Q q 0 0 612 792 re W n BT 9.6 TL/F178c54295-6309-47e9-898f-cce4f18a6349 8 Tf 1 0 0 1 511.352 777.6 Tm T* ET Q
endstream
