q q 1 0 0 1 78 719.8898 cm 0 0 0 rg BT 22 TL/F2 18 Tf 1 0 0 1 0 26 Tm (PL/SQL Practical No. 20 - Largest of Three)Tj T* (Numbers)Tj T* ET Q q 1 0 0 1 78 102.6898 cm 0 0 0 rg BT 8.8 TL/F3 8 Tf 1 0 0 1 36 581.6 Tm (QUESTION:)Tj T* T* (Write PL/SQL code to find the largest of three numbers.)Tj T* T* (------------------------------------------------------------)Tj T* (METHOD 1: USING IF-ELSIF-ELSE)Tj T* (------------------------------------------------------------)Tj T* T* (SET SERVEROUTPUT ON;)Tj T* T* (DECLARE)Tj T* (    num1 NUMBER := 10;)Tj T* (    num2 NUMBER := 25;)Tj T* (    num3 NUMBER := 15;)Tj T* (    largest NUMBER;)Tj T* (BEGIN)Tj T* (    IF num1 >= num2 AND num1 >= num3 THEN)Tj T* (        largest := num1;)Tj T* (    ELSIF num2 >= num1 AND num2 >= num3 THEN)Tj T* (        largest := num2;)Tj T* (    ELSE)Tj T* (        largest := num3;)Tj T* (    END IF;)Tj T* T* (    DBMS_OUTPUT.PUT_LINE\('Largest Number is: ' || largest\);)Tj T* (END;)Tj T* (/)Tj T* T* (------------------------------------------------------------)Tj T* (EXPECTED OUTPUT:)Tj T* T* (Largest Number is: 25)Tj T* T* (------------------------------------------------------------)Tj T* (METHOD 2: TAKING USER INPUT)Tj T* (------------------------------------------------------------)Tj T* T* (DECLARE)Tj T* (    num1 NUMBER;)Tj T* (    num2 NUMBER;)Tj T* (    num3 NUMBER;)Tj T* (    largest NUMBER;)Tj T* (BEGIN)Tj T* (    num1 := &Enter_First_Number;)Tj T* (    num2 := &Enter_Second_Number;)Tj T* (    num3 := &Enter_Third_Number;)Tj T* T* (    IF num1 >= num2 AND num1 >= num3 THEN)Tj T* (        largest := num1;)Tj T* (    ELSIF num2 >= num1 AND num2 >= num3 THEN)Tj T* (        largest := num2;)Tj T* (    ELSE)Tj T* (        largest := num3;)Tj T* (    END IF;)Tj T* T* (    DBMS_OUTPUT.PUT_LINE\('Largest Number is: ' || largest\);)Tj T* (END;)Tj T* (/)Tj T* T* (------------------------------------------------------------)Tj T* (VIVA POINTS:)Tj T* T* (1. IF-ELSIF-ELSE is used for decision making.)Tj T* (2. AND operator checks multiple conditions.)Tj T* (3. >= ensures correct comparison even if numbers are equal.)Tj T* (4. & is used for user input in SQL*Plus.)Tj T* (5. DBMS_OUTPUT.PUT_LINE displays output.)Tj T* ET Q Q q 0 0 612 792 re W n BT 9.6 TL/F1192038d7-fee0-492f-b6b9-c84946575edd 8 Tf 1 0 0 1 511.352 777.6 Tm T* ET Q
endstream
